## Overview

A personal, zero-cost, ad-free puzzle game suite built for mobile and desktop play.
Born out of frustration with commercial mobile puzzle apps riddled with unskippable
video ads, battery-draining telemetry, and aggressive monetization, this project
delivers an instant-loading, distraction-free environment for daily puzzle solving.

The suite combines a full-featured **Sudoku Classic** game and a retro-modern
**Minesweeper** under a unified architectural navigation shell powered by the
Sybilsedge Blueprint Design System.

## The Games

### Sudoku Classic

- **Mobile-First Responsive Grid** — 9x9 board with distinct 3x3 block borders, hairline cell dividers, and high-contrast styling optimized for touch screens.
- **Dual Input Modes** — 
  - *Cell-First*: Tap any cell, then tap a digit on the numeric keypad.
  - *Digit-First*: Select a digit on the keypad, then rapidly paint multiple cells across the board.
- **Dual-Layer Pencilmarks** — Supports both perimeter **Corner Notes** and clustered **Center Notes** for advanced candidate tracking.
- **Auto-Erasure** — Placing a confirmed digit automatically removes that candidate note from all peer cells in the same row, column, and 3x3 box.
- **Visual Assistance** — Row, column, and 3x3 block crosshair shading, same-digit highlight matching, and optional auto-check error indicators.
- **QQWing Puzzle Engine in Web Worker** — Generates boards off-thread via a dedicated Web Worker (`generator.worker.ts`) with background pre-caching. Guarantees 180° rotational symmetry and exactly one unique solution across logical difficulty tiers (Easy, Medium, Hard).
- **Move History & Persistence** — Full Undo/Redo stack, anti-peeking pause screen with timer freeze, and `localStorage` persistence across page reloads.

### Minesweeper

- **Retro-Modern Digital HUD** — LED-style segmented digital readouts for remaining mine count and elapsed time, paired with an interactive status face button.
- **Difficulty Presets** — Beginner (9x9, 10 mines), Intermediate (16x16, 40 mines), Expert (30x16, 99 mines), and custom dimension configurations.
- **Mobile Touch Controls** — Ergonomic thumb-friendly Dig vs. Flag mode toggle, long-press cell flagging, and chord clearing on revealed numbers.
- **Celebration Effects** — Integrated canvas confetti celebration upon successfully sweeping the grid.

## Tech Stack

- **Framework** — React 19 + TypeScript on Vite
- **Styling** — Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`)
- **Design System** — `@sybilsedge/blueprint-design`
- **Puzzle Engine** — `qqwing` compiled for browser execution
- **PWA & Offline** — `vite-plugin-pwa` and Workbox
- **Icons & Effects** — `lucide-react`, `canvas-confetti`
- **Hosting** — Cloudflare Pages via Wrangler

## Architecture

### Off-Thread Puzzle Generation

Generating valid Sudoku puzzles with guaranteed rotational symmetry and unique solutions
can be computationally intensive, especially on mobile hardware. Offloading the QQWing
solver and board generator to a dedicated Web Worker prevents frame drops on the main UI
thread, keeping input handling and animations running at 60/120fps.

### Offline PWA & Zero-Backend

The entire application runs purely client-side with zero backend dependencies.
Service worker caching via Workbox enables seamless offline play when installed to
an iOS or Android home screen (`display: standalone`). All gameplay state, active timers,
and settings persist to browser `localStorage`.

### Blueprint Design System

The application adopts the Sybilsedge Blueprint Design System, featuring:
- **Dark Cyberpunk Mode**: Deep black background, cyan glowing borders, and high-contrast monospace indicators.
- **Light Technical Blueprint Mode**: Crisp technical drawing styling reminiscent of architectural blueprints.
- **Classic Typography**: `Lora` serif font for the newspaper puzzle aesthetic paired with `Orbitron` and `JetBrains Mono` for technical readouts.

